## Architecture

### Core modules (`src/`)

| Module | Role |
|--------|------|
| `main.cpp` | Entry, `App::Run()` |
| `app.cpp` | Install/verify orchestration, worker threads, re-extract, `PostDone` |
| `gui.cpp` | Win32 UI, dark theme, status bar, file-log + re-extract windows |
| `drives.cpp` | USB/VHD/HDD enumeration, drive identity, capacity checks |
| `ventoy.cpp` | Download, extract, `VTOYCLI /I` or `/U` |
| `extract.cpp` | `7za` subprocess; full + selective (`@list`) extract |
| `verify.cpp` | Parallel MD5 verify, `check.log`, manifest load |
| `debug.cpp` | System/installer diagnostics written to `medicat_installer.log` |
| `bundle.cpp` | Extract embedded resources from exe |
| `download.cpp` | WinHTTP downloads (Ventoy, archive mirrors) |
| `offline.cpp` | Offline Ventoy/archive cache paths |
| `i18n.cpp` | `i18n::Tr()` — strings from build-generated header |
| `theme.cpp` | GDI+ dark controls, flat checkboxes, glow buttons |
| `log.cpp` | `medicat_installer.log` beside exe |

### Threading & UI updates

Long work runs on **detached `std::thread` workers** (`RunInstallThread`, `RunVerifyThread`). Never call GUI APIs from workers directly.

```cpp
// Worker posts to UI thread:
PostProgress(percent);                           // WM_MEDICAT_PROGRESS
PostExtractProgress(percent, file, resetLog);    // WM_MEDICAT_PROGRESS (extractUpdate)
PostStatusBar(text);                             // WM_MEDICAT_PROGRESS (statusOnly)
PostDone(success, message, title);               // WM_MEDICAT_DONE
```

**Status bar** — single line below progress bar. Any code updates it via `Gui::SetStatusBar` (UI thread) or `App::PostStatusBar` (workers). Includes Ventoy-on-drive detection (`status.ventoy_found` / `status.ventoy_not_on_drive`).

**File log popup** — optional listbox during extract/verify; status bar shows `status.extracting_file` with percent.

`Gui::SetBusy(true, BusyProgressMode::Verify|FileLog)` enables a 250ms timer that flushes pending file-log lines to the listbox.

**Re-extract prompt** — `WM_MEDICAT_REEXTRACT_PROMPT` opens a dedicated window (`Gui::OpenReExtractPrompt`) with failed-file list + **Re-extract** button; worker blocks on user choice via event.

### Key design principles

1. **Fail-safe** — confirm wipe/Ventoy/drive-letter changes; log everything
2. **Thread-safe UI** — workers post messages; GUI thread owns HWNDs
3. **Single-file distribution** — bundle 7za/7z/MD5 into exe; no sidecar copies
4. **Diagnostics on failure** — failure details + installer options appended to `medicat_installer.log` in `PostDone(false, …)`

## Ventoy UI & install logic

- **Detect on drive select:** `TestVentoyInstalled(drive)` — `ventoy` folder or VTOYEFI partition layout on the physical disk
- **No Ventoy on drive:** checkbox shows **Install Ventoy** — checked; format + Ventoy forced in getters (`RequiresForcedVentoyInstall`)
- **Ventoy present:** checkbox shows **Update Ventoy** — optional; format enabled (defaults unchecked on drive change)
- **Install thread:** `runVentoy = Gui::RunVentoyChecked()`; `/I` when `format || !ventoyInstalled`; `/U` for in-place upgrade otherwise
- Advanced: pin Ventoy version, GPT (`/GPT`), Secure Boot (`/NOSB`)

## Verify & re-extract

- Post-install and **Check USB Files** both run `VerifyMedicatFiles`
- On failure with failures list: re-extract window → `Extract7zArchiveSelective` (`7za … @reextract_list.txt`) → re-verify
- If still failing: `messages.verify_still_failed_after_reextract` (antivirus/firewall hint)
- After successful re-verify: show normal verification success message (not “run verify again”)

## Drive management (`drives.cpp`)

- Lists **USB removable** + **VHD/VHDX** (`BusTypeFileBackedVirtual`) by default
- **Show all drives** checkbox adds fixed HDD/SSD ≥ 30 GiB (`kMinDriveCapacityBytes`)
- Always hides `C:`
- Display: `H: "LABEL" (USB) - XGB free of YGB` when volume label exists
- `GetDriveIdentity` + `ResolveDriveLetterAfterVentoy` track disk numbers across Ventoy remounts

## Logging (beside exe)

Plain-text diagnostics only — future support upload is **`.log` / `.txt` only** (see `TODO.md`).

| File | When |
|------|------|
| `medicat_installer.log` | Every session (includes system/diagnostic sections; failure block on errors) |
| `extract.log` | 7za stdout/stderr during full extract |
| `reextract.log` | Selective re-extract (`7za @list`) |
| `check.log` | Per-file MD5 result during verify |
| `failed_files.txt` | Verification failures |

## i18n

- Source: `i18n/translations.json` (EN, ES, FR, PL, TR)
- Build codegen: `tools/i18n_codegen.py` → `src/i18n_generated.h`
- Usage: `i18n::Tr(L"key")` or `i18n::Tr(L"key", arg1, arg2)`
- Add keys to **all five languages** in `translations.json`; rebuild regenerates header

## Build

```bat
# x64
cmake -B build -G "Visual Studio 17 2022" -A x64
cmake --build build --config Release

# Win32
cmake -B build-x86 -G "Visual Studio 17 2022" -A Win32
cmake --build build-x86 --config Release
```

Output: `build/Release/MedicatInstaller.exe` or `build-x86/Release/MedicatInstaller-x86.exe`

**Bundle inputs:** `bin/7z/x64/7za.exe` (x64) or `bin/7z/x32/7za.exe` (Win32), `MedicatFiles.md5`

Defines: `INSTALLER_VERSION`, `MEDICAT_USB_VERSION` (CMake)

## Code conventions (C++)

- C++17, MSVC `/W4 /utf-8`, namespace `medicat`
- Minimize scope — match existing file style; no over-abstraction
- Wide strings (`std::wstring`) for Windows paths/UI; UTF-8 for log files
- Extended paths: `\\?\` prefix in `verify.cpp` for long manifest paths
- Listbox strings: persist in `fileLogDisplayLines_` — never pass temporaries to `LB_ADDSTRING`
- Verification workers: heap buffers for MD5 (`std::vector<BYTE>`), not large stack arrays

## When adding features

1. Read [`FEATURES.md`](FEATURES.md) for parity checklist vs PowerShell installer
2. Wire progress through `PostExtractProgress` / `PostStatusBar` / `onFileLog` callbacks
3. Add i18n keys for user-visible strings (all five languages)
4. Log via `log_->Info/Error/Debug` in `app.cpp`; module `onLog` for verify/ventoy
5. On new failure paths, ensure `PostDone(false, msg)` runs so failure diagnostics are logged
6. Do not commit `build/`, logs, `Ventoy2Disk/`, or `.7z` archives — see README **Contributing**

## Testing notes

- Requires **Administrator** (UAC manifest on exe)
- Test USB, VHD, and **Show all drives** (fixed disk) paths
- Test Ventoy-present vs absent drive: checkbox labels, forced format/install
- Verify: ~29k files / ~28 GB — re-extract path for selective failures
- Ventoy may remount drive under a different letter — confirm dialog must pass
- Release asset uploaded to GitHub tag (e.g. `3520` prerelease) via `gh release upload --clobber`

## Security

- Destructive ops require explicit confirmation (`wipe_confirm`, `ventoy_warning`)
- MD5 verify reads full file bytes; incomplete reads fail hash
- Internet required for Ventoy download (not for verify-only with bundled manifest); offline cache supported

## Legacy reference

PowerShell installer patterns (`pwsh` branch): `form.Invoke`, `Write-Log`, `medicat_download.log`, SevenZipSharp/7Zip4PowerShell. **Do not port PS patterns into C++** — use Win32 message posting and `7za` CLI instead.
